                <pb facs="0736" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg542"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi></head>
                <p>—No official minutes of the discussions in the Communiqué Subcommittee have been
                    found. Brown’s diary entry for July 31,
                    however, contains the following reference to this meeting: “… Communiqué
                    Committee met after Big Three meeting. We were well up with our work. …”
                        Brown’s report of August 1 to
                        Byrnes indicates that agreement was
                    reached in the Subcommittee on July 31 on the inclusion in the Communiqué of “a
                    single sentence stating Chiefs of Staffs of the three Governments conferred’ on
                    military matters of common interest.’ “See <ref target="#d1380">document No.
                        1380</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi> Cf. the following passage in
                        Brown’s diary entry for August 1: “In
                    first draft, I had confined military talks to affairs in Europe. Golunski wanted limitation stricken to appear
                    military talks included Japanese war.” Cf. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg585">page 585</ref>.</p>
            </div>
